/* ============================================================================
 * CollectionsMerchantTables.tsx — table rows the legacy page injected with JavaScript.
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * AUTO-GENERATED by hydrate_js_tables.py — regenerate rather than hand-edit.
 *
 * In 3.2.html these tables ship as an empty `<tbody id="…"></tbody>` and are
 * filled at runtime by vanilla JS (`tbody.innerHTML = data.map(…)`). A literal
 * markup conversion therefore reproduced an EMPTY table. Here the backing data
 * is lifted into `initialMockData` and the row template becomes JSX rendered
 * with `.map()`, so the rows are real React output and the table is
 * backend-ready: swap `initialMockData` for a query result and nothing else
 * changes.
 * ========================================================================== */
